        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 90-year-old female patient from 17th to 18th December 2024. She was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation consistent with COPD without signs of pneumonia. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. She improved satisfactorily and was discharged home in stable condition. Please ensure follow-up including review of her inhaler technique and continuation of her maintenance therapy. I remain available for any further queries. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
